@@ -86,3 +86,11 @@ The descriptor is a separate physical metadata-pool frame. It has no routed Meta
 An already-open handle authenticates the descriptor when acquiring a new metadata snapshot too; failure releases that new pin instead of allowing subsequent snapshots to continue through ROW after open-time validation. Descriptor reads use the file view's construction-time database ID, avoiding a race with writer rebinding of the mutable routing Superblock. The fixed charged PROFILE registry records `native_graph.read.metadata_decodes.hybrid_descriptor` (current-thread cumulative decode attempts). Resource caps are unchanged; registry/staging bounds derive from actual entry count.
 
 The 4096-membership ceiling applies to one explicit conversion plan, not the lifetime capacity of a converted group. The group header records the actual count in its declared u32 field; ordinary writes must retain existing dynamic-property support and checked count arithmetic. Conversion/reverse-conversion still refuses work above its bounded plan, rather than truncating, silently splitting publication, or treating 4096 as a permanent schema limit.
+
+## Extension envelope preparation
+
+The uninstalled R3.2 extension codec uses a 48-byte ZYHE (`0x4548595A`) envelope, version 1: magic u32 at 0, version u16 at 4, owner kind u8 at 6, mode u8 at 7 (1=inline, 2=LargeValue reference), native owner ID u64 at 8, token u32 at 16, body bytes u32 at 20, semantic generation u64 at 24, reserved-zero 32..47. Inline mode contains exactly one existing canonical PropertyValue; missing has no extension/selector, while NULL has the canonical NULL value. Authenticate outer owner/token and extension<=group<=descriptor<=snapshot; a referenced logical generation must not exceed extension generation.
+
+Large mode reuses the existing LargeValueRefCodec and `application/vnd.zyx.entity-property-root` media, with the owner-neutral payload constrained to exactly one token/value. Both directory token and entry token must match the outer token; multiple fields, trailing data, wrong kind/media or future identity reject. Existing LargeValueStore must authenticate manifest, chunks and content hash before supplying bytes; this envelope decoder does not authenticate content by itself. Do not create a separate whole-row copy or treat an arbitrary same-media row as one field. Equal one-field payloads may share immutable contents across owners through existing deduplication and exact retirement rules.
+
+The complete extension record must fit the actual destination limit and at most 3952 bytes (4032 owner payload minus 64 slotted header minus 16 slot bytes). A packed B+Tree key also needs its ordered owner/token prefix, packed framing, page header/slots and internal separator capacity; the future map planner must lower its record limit accordingly, never assume a 3952-byte record fits a B+Tree key. Charge the 48-byte envelope and any additional directory/value framing in total native costs. Destination and canonical encoding workspace use caller-owned PMR; reference media capacity and decoded value/directory allocations require separate retained reservations. The charged conversion plan can emit only actual inline-extension members, rejecting column-source members and oversized values. This codec does not install variable-map routing, allocate data IDs, publish large values or remove nonempty-root guards.
